Explanation for binary files inside source package according to
? https://lists.debian.org/debian-devel/2013/09/msg00332.html

The files are helping the testing of the sources, serving as a reference.
Their content can be retrieved with no technical difficulty. These files
are accompanied by cognate .R files, which are R scripts to create them.
These in turn efer to data packages
? maqcExpression4plex
https://www.bioconductor.org/packages/release/data/experiment/html/maqcExpression4plex.html
? pd.huex.1.0.st.v2
https://www.bioconductor.org/packages/release/data/annotation/html/pd.huex.1.0.st.v2.html
? pd.hugene.1.0.st.v1
https://www.bioconductor.org/packages/release/data/annotation/html/pd.hugene.1.0.st.v1.html
that are provided by yet other R packages that we do
not redistribute because of a focus on function, less on data, and these
packages are big.

None of these R or .rda files, are required for the use of the oligo
package.

